                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being observable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2609e4a9-b094-3dbc-b985-e26e688963ce",
                        "entry_id": "4c59a7db-524b-3c00-93d4-cb6dd5dc3714",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A measure of the extent to which something is observable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "061fb345-7200-3522-a95a-6da2bc3f7ac1",
                        "entry_id": "4c59a7db-524b-3c00-93d4-cb6dd5dc3714",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The ability to collect data about the execution of distributed programs, especially the interaction among its components."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3441f87d-4b85-4c28-8dbb-2ac44a798ee4",
                                "sense_id": "061fb345-7200-3522-a95a-6da2bc3f7ac1",
                                "text": "“In 2018, we saw many companies that are cloud-native and in the tech sector talking about observability,” he said. “Last year, we saw this becoming more mainstream, with large organizations adopting cloud-native technologies and becoming interested in observability.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ff01731-7132-42a8-8dec-9ad2a9e55e4e",
                                "sense_id": "061fb345-7200-3522-a95a-6da2bc3f7ac1",
                                "text": "Observability is defined as the ability to understand the internal state of a system by only looking at external outputs of the system. […] Observability builds on monitoring and enables you to gain insights about the internal state of your application."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68fac92b-c24a-4767-b466-57392c918c84",
                                "sense_id": "061fb345-7200-3522-a95a-6da2bc3f7ac1",
                                "text": "In other words, SREs are directly responsible for the effectiveness of observability."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
